---
---

<section id="research" style="position:relative;padding:96px 64px;background:transparent;border-top:1px solid var(--rulesoft)">
    <div style="max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto">
      <span style="font-family:var(--fmono);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--teal)">Research</span>
      <h2 style="font-weight:700;font-size:42px;line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin-top:12px;color:var(--t1);max-width:820px">The method, and the benchmark we are building.</h2>
      <p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--t2);max-width:680px;margin-top:14px">A claims-validation tool should hold itself to the same standard. Here is how the review works, and how it will be measured: method first, numbers when they exist.</p>

      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;margin-top:44px">
        <a class="rcard" href="demo.html" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:14px;padding:26px;background:var(--surface-paper);text-decoration:none">
          <span style="font-family:var(--fmono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold)">How it works</span>
          <h3 style="font-weight:600;font-size:22px;color:var(--t1);margin-top:12px">Decompose, search, grade</h3>
          <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--t2);margin-top:10px;flex:1">Telotia breaks a document into atomic claims, matches each against the corpus you supplied, not the open web, and returns a graded verdict linked to its source.</p>
          <span class="rarrow" style="font-family:var(--fmono);font-size:12px;color:var(--t3);margin-top:18px;transition:color .2s var(--ease)">See the steps →</span>
        </a>
        <a class="rcard" href="workspace.html" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:14px;padding:26px;background:var(--surface-paper);text-decoration:none">
          <span style="font-family:var(--fmono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold)">Why a corpus</span>
          <h3 style="font-weight:600;font-size:22px;color:var(--t1);margin-top:12px">Built on evidence you can check</h3>
          <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--t2);margin-top:10px;flex:1">The showcase runs on a fixed, trusted body of research that stands on its own, demonstrating the general capability: any document, any trusted corpus you choose.</p>
          <span class="rarrow" style="font-family:var(--fmono);font-size:12px;color:var(--t3);margin-top:18px;transition:color .2s var(--ease)">See it run →</span>
        </a>
        <a class="rcard" href="consult.html" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:14px;padding:26px;background:radial-gradient(circle at 18% 12%,rgba(232,169,143,.08),transparent 42%),var(--surface-raised);text-decoration:none">
          <span style="font-family:var(--fmono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold)">In progress</span>
          <h3 style="font-weight:600;font-size:22px;color:var(--t1);margin-top:12px">An open benchmark</h3>
          <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--t2);margin-top:10px;flex:1">An open benchmark, measuring how well Telotia separates supported claims from unsupported ones, is in progress. The method and results will be published here, including where it falls short.</p>
          <span class="rarrow" style="font-family:var(--fmono);font-size:12px;color:var(--t3);margin-top:18px;transition:color .2s var(--ease)">Get in touch →</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
